{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540678-dragons-of-darkness","id":1540678,"title":"Dragons of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-18T18:43:44-07:00","id":1540678,"title":"Dragons of Darkness","content":"How powerful are the different types of dragons found within the world of darkness? I know there are the zemei, the bygones, and those found within the deep of the dreaming. How do they compare to the main game lines like vampire, werewolf, mage, and changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T19:03:15-07:00","id":1540680,"title":"","content":"Werewolf's corner:<br /> <br /> Zmei are calibrated to give a hard fight to elder and legendary Garou, so they range from horribly powerful stat-wise to simply just not being described by stats, depending on your interpretation of various later material in comparison to Rage Across Russia.<br /> <br /> The Wani, who are the patrons of the Nagah, are Incarnae. Flat-out more powerful than anything with stats.<br /> <br /> Mokole can be incredibly huge in Archid, and have the potential to learn mountains of Gift and ritual lore to become capable of some truly awe-inspiring and frightening feats, but they are ultimately still intended to interface at the player character level. They can start out Godzilla-sized, however, and push it further in certain Near Realms like Pangaea, where they can become notably large even when compared with the Elder Serpent.<br /> <br /> Said Elder Serpent of Pangaea is said to be a fragment of the uncorrupted Wyrm. No one's really sure how powerful they are, exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T12:21:44-07:00","id":1540720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540678-dragons-of-darkness#post1540678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How powerful are the different types of dragons found within the world of darkness? I know there are the zemei, the bygones, and those found within the deep of the dreaming. How do they compare to the main game lines like vampire, werewolf, mage, and changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can technically be as powerful as you'd need them to be.<br /> <br /> Like Saur Ops mentioned above, plenty of them could be Incarnae, meaning they rank like Antidiluvian vampires in terms of power. Of those that Mages could interact would probably be the mythical reflections found in the Astral Plane, like Jormungandr, Tiamat and similar myths.<br /> <br /> In the Dreaming you can also find similar divine Dragons, or at least highly powerful. The dragon Smaug from Lord of the Rings would be a good example, although in the case of Smaug he would probably be more on the range of a vampiric Methuselah rather than a 3rd generation anti.<br /> <br /> Then you can find everything in between; bygones are probably not so Godlike, albeit still being quite formidable, but some may be more &quot;player level&quot; based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T23:34:53-07:00","id":1540751,"title":"","content":"I mean, from Mage's standpoint, Zmei are bygones, but also quite powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T10:53:34-07:00","id":1540964,"title":"","content":"Bygones suffer from the effects of unbelief and have to deal with Consensus. Zmei, and indeed Wyrm-spawned creatures generally, don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T11:01:02-07:00","id":1540965,"title":"","content":"True Dragons in dark ages-mage are obscene. On top of some pretty brutal powers as a dragon they're rocking up as a master tier verbenna spellcaster on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T15:17:54-07:00","id":1540974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1540678-dragons-of-darkness?p=1540965#post1540965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Dragons in dark ages-mage are obscene. On top of some pretty brutal powers as a dragon they're rocking up as a master tier verbenna spellcaster on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have the stats for that dragon or where I could find them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T15:25:46-07:00","id":1540975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=